{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/571389-werewolves-and-angels-demons","id":571389,"title":"Werewolves and Angels/Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-28T08:25:08-07:00","id":571389,"title":"Werewolves and Angels/Demons","content":"I'm curious as to how capable werewolves would be at sensing or spotting Angels or Demons, would anyone have a better idea then me on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T09:56:26-07:00","id":571593,"title":"","content":"Not especially. Angelic ephemera doesn't exist on the same &quot;wavelength&quot; of Twilight as spiritual ephemera (similarly to how the Ghost Eater Numen indicates that spirits in Twilight can't perceive ghosts in Twilight normally), so the ability to perceive spirits in Twilight doesn't confer angel sight. (Do Uratha have that ability natively anyway, now that I look for it and can't find it?) Uratha lack the demonic and stigmatic ability to see through concealment infrastructure too, although they could use an appropriate sensory power to trigger a Clash of Wills and try to pierce through.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Insight's Scent the Unnatural Facet can pick a demon out of a crowd, but demons are good at blocking abilities like that \u2014 even on a successful use, the demon gets to counter-roll to try to &quot;spoof&quot; and fool the power. It'll work on angels too, and angels do not have the ability to spoof.<br /> <br /> In general, Uratha without special experience with angels or demons are likely, I think, to notice them in situations where they could be mistaken for spirits or Claimed of industrial aspect \u2014 unless, of course, they witness a demon switch between multiple Covers, which is a strong indicator that they fall into the &quot;other&quot; category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T10:12:25-07:00","id":571624,"title":"","content":"Not very. Wolves aren't very capable at spotting ghosts in Twilight without the Glory aspect of the Death Gifts (Barghest). Naturally, a Materialized ghost is another matter, and there's going to be a trail of hints, both through the news and via the Shadow, that lead to any haunted spot. But directly sensing them? Not so much. There's no reason angels should be any different than ghosts, and any appropriate Gifts aren't exactly common. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Unchained? First, you'd need a way to sense other supernaturals, since demons naturally smell like their Covers, nothing obvious. So, that means you'd need Scent the Unnatural (Purity aspect of Insight Gift), be within range, and have reason to spend the essence to activate the Gift. Then, the demon gets to Spoof, no Clash of Wills. If the demon has an Exploited Gadget, the Gift would pick up on that, but not the embedded ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> As you can see, the chances are very pretty low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:59:22-07:00","id":571723,"title":"","content":"*nods* That helps a great deal, thank you both for the information. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}